 things! Do not worry even a little bit / about incoming food, seeking it. / In the mountain-rice fields, the kindled fires of the guards, like conch shells, / shine with light like perfect gems, dispelling the dense darkness. / He is the lord of such a hard land, Pittan of the strong horse! / His spear that conquers fierce battles, and his lord, / Kothai of great and generous giving, / and even the hostile kings, may they all live for a long time!","translation":"Place the pots on the hearth! Cook the rice! Ensure the toddy never runs low! Let the singing dancers adorned with bright jewels wear garlands! Do all these things in abundance. Do not worry even a little about where the next meal will come from. In his land, the fires lit by those guarding the mountain rice-fields shine like polished gems, dispelling the dense darkness like white conch shells. He is Pittan, lord of the rugged hills, who rides a swift horse. May his spear that triumphs in fierce battles, his sovereign lord Kothai of boundless generosity, and even his enemy kings who oppose him, live long!","modern":"அடுப்பில் உலைகளை ஏற்றுங்கள்! சோறு சமைங்கள்! கள் குறைந்துவிடாமல் பார்த்துக் கொள்ளுங்கள்! ஒளிவீசும் அணிகலன்களை அணிந்த பாடிவரும் விறலியர் மாலைகளைச் சூடிக் கொள்ளட்டும்! இத்தகைய பல காரியங்களைச் செய்யுங்கள். உணவு எங்கிருந்து வரும் என்று சிறிதும் கவலைப்பட வேண்டாம். மலைநெல் வயல்களைக் காப்பவர்கள் மூட்டும் தீயானது, அடர்ந்த இருளை அகற்றும் ஒளிவீசும் திருந்திய மணிகளைப் போலவும் சங்கு போலவும் விளங்கும் வன்புல நாட்டை உடையவன், வலிய குதிரையை உடைய பிட்டன் ஆவான். அவனது போரை வெல்லும் வேலும், அவனது தலைவனான கொடையாளி கோதையும், அவனை எதிர்க்கும் பகை மன்னர்களும் நீண்ட காலம் வாழ்க!","explanation":"The poet Vaṭamaṇṇakkaṉ Tāmōtaraṉār is addressing his fellow artists and the household in praise of the chieftain Piṭṭaṅkoṟṟaṉ. Having arrived at the court of this generous patron, the poet enthusiastically commands everyone to feast, cook rice, drink toddy, and adorn themselves without any anxiety about the future. This poem belongs to the Pāṭāṇ tiṇai, which focuses on praising a patron's exploits and generosity. The imagery of the guards' fires in the mountain rice fields shining like precious gems and conch shells in the deep darkness highlights the richness and security of Pittan's hilly territory. Key words include 'பரியல் வெண்டா' (do not worry), 'வன்புல நாடன்' (lord of the rugged land), and 'பிட்டன்' (Pittan).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,0.8],[0.8,1.3],[1.3,1.7],[1.7,2.4],[2.4,2.8],[3.0,3.44],[3.48,3.6],[3.6,5.0],[5.0,5.3],[5.3,5.5],[5.5,5.9],[5.9,6.8],[6.8,7.3],[7.3,7.6],[7.6,8.0],[8.0,8.6],[8.9,9.2],[9.2,10.1],[10.1,10.4],[10.4,10.66],[10.66,10.66],[10.66,10.66],[10.66,12.2],[12.2,13.3],[13.3,13.85],[14.06,14.25],[14.25,14.7],[14.7,15.8],[15.8,15.8],[15.8,16.4],[16.4,16.7],[17.72,18.42],[18.42,18.42],[18.42,19.02],[19.02,19.62],[19.62,20.09],[20.56,20.72],[20.72,21.22],[21.22,22.22],[22.22,22.32],[22.32,22.82],[22.82,23.32]],"female":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,0.8],[0.8,1.3],[1.3,1.8],[1.8,2.2],[2.2,3.4],[3.4,4.0],[4.06,4.4],[4.4,5.6],[5.6,6.0],[6.0,6.3],[6.3,6.6],[6.6,7.9],[7.9,8.0],[8.0,8.8],[8.8,9.1],[9.1,9.68],[9.68,9.68],[9.68,11.4],[11.4,11.5],[11.5,12.12],[12.12,12.9],[12.9,13.0],[13.3,13.47],[13.5,14.8],[14.8,15.4],[15.47,15.89],[15.89,16.4],[16.4,17.6],[17.6,17.6],[17.6,18.2],[18.2,18.5],[19.56,20.26],[20.26,20.26],[20.26,20.96],[20.96,21.46],[21.46,21.46],[21.46,21.46],[21.46,21.46],[21.46,21.46],[21.46,25.16],[25.16,25.36],[25.36,25.96]]}}